For each Licensor's material, the copyright notice in the MIT text includes
that Licensor's applicable accompanying copyright notices.

Conversion requires no payment, application, additional permission,
replacement license file, or other action by a recipient or Licensor.

Conversion covers all material made available under this License for the
same Project before or on the Conversion Date, including earlier versions,
archived releases, redistributed copies, and covered portions of forks
and derivative works. It applies even if that material is omitted from
the stable release or a copy still displays an earlier version number.

Material first made available under this License for the same Project
after the Conversion Date is licensed under MIT immediately. This
License makes no grant for future material offered only under other terms.

From the Conversion Date onward, the MIT License alone governs subsequent
use, copying, modification, distribution, sublicensing, sale, and other
exercise of the copyright permissions granted here. The noncommercial
condition and all additional development-license conditions cease to apply
to those acts. You may distribute converted Software with the applicable
copyright notices and MIT text without retaining the development terms.

The future MIT grant survives termination of the development license.
Conversion does not retroactively authorize a violation committed before
the Conversion Date or waive a claim arising from that violation, but a
prior violation does not prevent the MIT grant from taking effect.

